WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:17.899
In preparation for most sermons, and in particular this one, I read a lot of other

00:00:17.899 --> 00:00:20.449
people's thoughts on this text. 

00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:22.029
I read other sermons,

00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:24.770
I skimmed many commentaries.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:29.260
Most of them had really cute titles,

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.169
like "Quite a Catch,"

00:00:31.169 --> 00:00:33.130
"Fishing for Christ,"

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.560
or-- by far the most popular--

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.050
"Gone Fishin'." 

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:43.890
Well, those get a little cheesy for my taste, but the
one that caught my attention was

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.130
"Get Outta Here." Hm. 

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:51.860
I don't like to judge a book by its cover,
or a commentary by its title, so I read on, 

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.980
and discovered that Will Willimon, Methodist bishop,
had written about this very Gospel text a

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.440
few years ago in the Christian century. 

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.370
He commented on how the crowd was pushing
in on Jesus,

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:08.340
finally starting to maybe understand what
he was about, attracted to his sermons and his 

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.370
words,

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.550
but there was Simon. 

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.290
Simon, witness to this crazy unbelievable
miracle,

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.630
and all Simon could say is, 

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.480
"Get away from me, Lord!"

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.690
Or-- Willimon's translation--

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.920
"Get outta here!"

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.460
Well, "get out of here" seems, maybe, the most
appropriate response,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:35.810
because what do we normally say when we hear
the crazy, unbelievable, too good to be true

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.680
miracles in the Gospel?

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.290
Get outta here. 

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:43.159
Or what do we say when we hear Jesus
calling us

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:45.550
out to the deep water?

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.160
Get outta here. 

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.990
A sarcastic yet quite honest response that
we might find ourselves saying quite often

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.600
to the call of God. 

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.530
When I was a freshman in college,

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.159
my chaplain pulled me aside

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:01.580
the beginning of the second semester and said, 

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.010
"Have you considered seminary?" 

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:09.699
Well, it had been a long semester of fishing
for the right major,

00:02:09.699 --> 00:02:11.039
not catching

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:12.159
anything,

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:17.979
cleaning my nets after final exams, wondering
if all of the work was just in vain. 

00:02:17.979 --> 00:02:22.909
But I was also very content in my little small
boat with my Communications major and my tightly

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.449
held dreams to be on the radio someday.

00:02:26.449 --> 00:02:27.530
But I think

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.130
God was speaking through Chaplain Brian that
day when he nudged me to consider exploring

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.469
ministry.

00:02:33.469 --> 00:02:37.059
"Well, have you thought about seminary?" he said
again. 

00:02:37.059 --> 00:02:41.139
My quick and baffled answer was, "Uh, no."

00:02:41.139 --> 00:02:41.849
Translation:

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:43.700
get outta here. 

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.939
And then I had to also ask,

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:48.929
"What's seminary?"

00:02:48.929 --> 00:02:54.479
He explained more, and I said, "Uh, no. No, thank you.
I'm very content in my small boat with my communications

00:02:54.479 --> 00:02:58.149
major and my tightly held dreams to be on the radio."

00:02:58.149 --> 00:03:03.739
But after each semester, when I was cleaning
my nets, wondering if my work was in vain,

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:07.250
he would find yet another creative way to
drop this hint, 

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.479
subtly or not so subtly. 

00:03:09.479 --> 00:03:11.819
So we were cleaning up from an evening service,

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:17.520
he would say, "Well, we are offering a course
this winter on exploring careers in ministry

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.839
in case you're interested."

00:03:19.839 --> 00:03:22.619
My silence became my way of saying, 

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:24.649
get outta here. 

00:03:24.649 --> 00:03:29.269
But simultaneously there was this nagging
curiosity growing,

00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:34.049
and I hardly noticed that I was gradually
and repeatedly being invited

00:03:34.049 --> 00:03:37.169
to go out to the deep water.

00:03:37.169 --> 00:03:42.439
This invitation came not only from Chaplain Brian but another voice that I didn't understand--

00:03:42.439 --> 00:03:45.150
a voice that promised risk and also hope,

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:49.479
a voice that assured me I wasn't going to
do it alone.

00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:53.109
But this pull out to deep water was a much slower
process than

00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:54.999
for Simon and company.

00:03:54.999 --> 00:03:56.819
It took years.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:58.949
It's still going on.

00:03:58.949 --> 00:04:02.839
I don't think deep water is a place we can
ever get too comfortable;

00:04:02.839 --> 00:04:06.139
there're too many dangers out there, too much
unknown. But

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:07.010
before we know it,

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.799
the tide has pushed us back to the shore,

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:13.779
back to a place of the safe, secure, shallow
water.

00:04:13.779 --> 00:04:17.489
Until God once again calls us out into the
deep, and we have to decide

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:18.459
yet again

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:21.229
how we will respond.

00:04:21.229 --> 00:04:24.830
I'm not going to bore you with the rest of
the story of how I got into ministry,

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.969
and I do want to make it really clear

00:04:26.969 --> 00:04:31.949
that following the call of Jesus does not necessarily
mean pursuing professional ministry.

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:36.909
In fact, another mentor in college turned to me
when he heard I was considering this, and said

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.130
"If you can do anything else

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.880
besides be a pastor, you should do it."

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.120
He was a little burned out himself.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.720
But he was also

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.710
saying, if God is inviting you

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:50.010
to the deep waters of some other calling,

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.610
you better get in that boat--

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:57.069
the boat made for you.

00:04:57.069 --> 00:05:02.389
Well, when it comes to the call of the disciples,
by the lake shore, each of our four Gospels

00:05:02.389 --> 00:05:08.519
tells a similar story but emphasizes different
details, which I think are really important.

00:05:08.519 --> 00:05:13.380
In Matthew and Mark, we hear a very short
story about the call of Simon and Andrew,

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.819
brothers called to be disciples.

00:05:15.819 --> 00:05:18.389
Jesus gets right to the point. He walks up
to them.

00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:20.919
They are fishing off the shore.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:25.250
And he just says, "Follow me. I'll make you fish for people." That's it.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.930
They dropped their nets.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.649
Jesus continues down the shore

00:05:28.649 --> 00:05:30.780
to James and John.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.320
"Follow me. I'll make you fish for people."

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.790
They drop their nets.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.620
That's it.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.279
In the Gospel of John--

00:05:37.279 --> 00:05:39.359
never as brief--

00:05:39.359 --> 00:05:43.069
Jesus stands on the shore and calls out to
the disciples out there in the fishing  

00:05:43.069 --> 00:05:45.519
boat, "Hey, have you caught any fish?"

00:05:45.519 --> 00:05:46.849
"No."

00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:50.340
"Well just try throwing the nets in on the other side of the boat."

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.439
And they were full.

00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:53.530
That's how it happens

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.059
for John.

00:05:56.059 --> 00:06:00.150
And instead of Simon saying "get outta here,"
or some version of that,

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.440
Simon actually gets out of there himself.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.729
He is so stunned in the Gospel of John that

00:06:04.729 --> 00:06:07.529
he jumps out of the boat. 

00:06:07.529 --> 00:06:08.489
But Luke

00:06:08.489 --> 00:06:11.919
chooses to tell it another way.

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:13.889
Jesus gets into the boat

00:06:13.889 --> 00:06:15.569
with Simon.

00:06:15.569 --> 00:06:20.499
Jesus is back on the beach in the other Gospels.
He's in the boat in Luke.

00:06:20.499 --> 00:06:23.500
And he tells Simon to row out to the deep water,

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.949
the only time in the four Gospels that it involves
deep water. 

00:06:27.949 --> 00:06:32.199
Simon explains they've been fishing all
night and haven't caught a thing,

00:06:32.199 --> 00:06:35.030
but agrees to give it a try.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:38.400
And they instantly catch a bunch of fish. 

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.909
And we know that Simon is so in awe of the
presence of Jesus that he tells him,

00:06:42.909 --> 00:06:44.469
"Get out of here!"

00:06:44.469 --> 00:06:49.039
He feels unworthy to be in the presence of
God, in the presence of this miracle worker,

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:50.979
Jesus. 

00:06:50.979 --> 00:06:52.790
But instead of Jesus

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.150
just saying,

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:58.079
"Follow me" as we hear in Matthew and Mark,

00:06:58.079 --> 00:06:59.810
Jesus instead tells Simon,

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.749
"Do not be afraid. 

00:07:01.749 --> 00:07:03.190
From now on you will be

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.340
catching people."

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.870
So the gift of having these four slightly
different versions in the Gospels is that

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:13.090
we have at least four different lenses through
which we can hear

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.099
and see this story.

00:07:16.099 --> 00:07:22.119
In this year of reading Luke's Gospel together,
in this day of hearing Luke's miraculous fishing

00:07:22.119 --> 00:07:22.990
story,

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.180
Luke's lens

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:28.239
gives us some unique ways to consider discipleship.

00:07:28.239 --> 00:07:32.550
Now discipleship is one of those words we
throw around a lot here at this church.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.319
We sing about being called disciples of
Jesus.

00:07:35.319 --> 00:07:41.549
We pray for strength to do it. We hear texts
like today's about the disciples of Jesus.

00:07:41.549 --> 00:07:42.680
And yet,

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:47.909
discipleship might not be one of those words
you say ever outside of these walls.

00:07:47.909 --> 00:07:49.980
The twelve disciples can be put on such a

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.759
pedestal in our minds,

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:53.200
that we forget just how

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.799
imperfect, just how much like us,

00:07:55.799 --> 00:07:58.049
they are.

00:07:58.049 --> 00:08:00.269
Thus the task of discipleship

00:08:00.269 --> 00:08:02.010
can seem so inflated

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:03.300
and become one of those

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:08.360
"I'll never get it right and may as well not try"
kinds of things.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.889
And yet we are somehow drawn back here,

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:12.990
to this place, to this text,

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.589
to ask what it means

00:08:14.589 --> 00:08:16.909
for us.

00:08:16.909 --> 00:08:19.360
Luke's story of the miraculous catch of fish

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.150
and the invitation to Simon

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.810
to take up a different kind of fishing

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:29.379
might be able to help us decode the loaded word of
discipleship. 

00:08:29.379 --> 00:08:30.160
Now I hate

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.710
tidy three-point sermons.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:37.600
But somehow I have distilled this next section
down into three tidy points. Ok. 

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:38.669
Discipleship

00:08:38.669 --> 00:08:39.610
in Luke. 

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.080
Number one:

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.350
Jesus asks his disciples to go into the deep
water

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.540
but goes with them. 

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.880
That is key.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.029
If discipleship

00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:53.440
means getting into your metaphorical boat
and going into your metaphorical deep waters,

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.400
then it is crucial to remember that for Luke,

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.670
the deep water happens only

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:03.480
when Jesus gets in the boat with the disciples.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.960
Where do you sense the presence of God?

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:10.070
Is it sometimes in those moments when you
experience risk

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.390
or stretching out of your comfort zone?

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.230
Jesus rarely calls us

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.030
to the convenient,

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:20.160
comfortable, complacent shallow waters.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:26.000
But Jesus doesn't call you to places where
he hasn't gone or isn't willing to go.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.089
Your deep water is going to be different

00:09:28.089 --> 00:09:30.850
than anyone else's deep water.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:35.460
Being here this morning might feel like you're
being thrown in the deep end.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.590
Completely unfamiliar, this might feel terribly
risky,

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:42.520
and for other people this might feel right at
home.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:45.350
Regardless of what the deep water is for you,

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.450
here's the truth for Luke:

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.560
if Jesus calls you to the deep water

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:53.000
he's going with you.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:53.860
Second:

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.590
Jesus asks his disciples to be honest,

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:59.030
and then calms fears. 

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.959
So discipleship is being

00:10:00.959 --> 00:10:01.560
honest

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:02.980
with Jesus.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:07.920
Simon doesn't pretend to be all holy
when he witnessed the miracle of the fish.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.900
Instead he just blurted out his

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:10.379
honest,

00:10:10.379 --> 00:10:12.010
fear-filled truth,

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:17.500
acknowledging that he didn't feel worthy
to be in the presence of Jesus.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.600
Also,

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.670
Jesus senses Simon's fear

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:23.440
in this response.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.240
Simon says, "Get out of here," and Jesus says,

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.420
"Don't be afraid."

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:33.400
Jesus can take your honesty even if it
seems rude.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:37.300
So if you sense that God might be nudging you in
some direction that you just can't imagine

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.140
going,

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:43.190
you may as well be honest. Wrestle it out with
God a bit.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.860
"Get out of here" for Simon

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:51.610
was his honest and actually pretty humble response
to nets so miraculously full of fish.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.310
When Jesus gets in the boat,

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.940
you won't be able to hide very much,

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:59.010
but your honesty will be matched with Christ's

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.960
fear-calming comfort and presence. 

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:04.640
And third: 

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.509
discipleship might invite you to leave
those nets behind,

00:11:08.509 --> 00:11:09.990
even as they are bursting 

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:12.370
with fish. 

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:13.830
Yeah.

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:18.430
This-- the disciples just leave their nets and follow
him, and this might sound even

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.860
scarier than the deep water. 

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.380
It's not logical

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.740
for the disciples to leave.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:30.940
They did not sit down and calculate how much that was going to cost them in losses.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:35.660
Logic was left way back there in the shallow
water a long time ago for them, though. 

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:40.980
It wasn't logical to follow Jesus out into the
deep water after a night of pointless fishing.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:45.200
It wasn't logical for them to leave their nets
bursting with 

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.620
finance and security.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.339
It was not logical,

00:11:49.339 --> 00:11:50.720
but Jesus

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.430
isn't logical.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:53.149
Discipleship

00:11:53.149 --> 00:11:55.490
might not be logical.

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.169
It's not a matter of just

00:11:57.169 --> 00:12:02.460
rearranging the pieces of our lives to make
room for God somehow.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.320
Discipleship

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:07.320
is being willing to walk away from all
those pieces

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.620
to follow Christ. 

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.450
Youu might not be called to leave family

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:16.570
or business or goals behind.

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.230
But discipleship

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.299
calls us to be willing to do that,

00:12:20.299 --> 00:12:23.060
or at least keep all of those pieces

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:25.910
in perspective.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:30.900
Discipleship is a willingness to follow
Jesus into the unknown,

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:36.130
and I know that's terribly vague and abstract,
especially for those of you grasping for

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:40.360
some clear picture of what your future's
going to hold.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.780
You list pros and cons,

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.990
we get everyone's expert opinion about what
we should do, we try to please family members

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.750
or advisers--

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:54.430
but all of this may not help you, in the end,
to feel certain. 

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:56.310
Poet Wendell Berry writes,

00:12:56.310 --> 00:13:00.220
"It may be that when we no longer know what to do,

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:02.910
we have come to our real work."

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:09.910
And that when we no longer know which way
to go, we have come to our real journey.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.590
So all I'm saying is

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.650
that there may be a time

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:18.000
when you feel drawn to do something for reasons
you cannot explain,

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.370
in ways that don't make financial sense or
please other people,

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.660
and that might be exactly what

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:25.550
you are supposed to do. Amen. 

